        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 回来",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "回来 — huílái — \"to come back\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "我下个月五号回来 wǒ xià ge yuè wǔ hào huílái — I'll be back on the fifth of next month."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 回 (huí) — six strokes: a large frame, a small 口 inside it, and the bar that closes the large frame last. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "回来 (huílái) is built from 回 (huí) 'to turn back' and 来 'to come', both inherited from Middle Chinese, hwoj and loj (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'to turn round'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
